From: steamac <steamac@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] MSL: evaluate sample-rate inputs at explicit sample positions

STEAMAC-8J reproduces on M1 as missing llvm.agx2.sample.itrproj.1xf
for sample-qualified projected sampling, including ordinary texture and
compare samples in all math modes. Explicit sample-position offset
interpolation avoids the broken fusion without changing division or
interpolation positions. Keep native behavior by default; affect only
Sample inputs and explicit InterpolateAtSample when the option is enabled.
Preserve flat inputs, composite/helper paths, and per-sample invocation.

--- a/spirv_msl.hpp
+++ b/spirv_msl.hpp
@@ -543,6 +543,11 @@
 		// expected to be needed until the bug is fixed in Metal; it is provided as an option
 		// so it can be enabled only when the bug is present.
 		bool sample_dref_lod_array_as_grad = false;
+
+		// Avoid broken sample-rate projected-texture fusion on affected Metal backends.
+		// Evaluate sample-qualified inputs at get_sample_position(sample_id) using
+		// pull-model offset interpolation, preserving the original arithmetic.
+		bool sample_rate_interpolation_as_offset = false;
 
 		// Apply a workaround to prevent uses of bitwise not from crashing the AMD backend compiler
 		bool bitwise_not_causes_ice = false;
@@ -1580,6 +1585,8 @@
 	std::string to_vertex_input_value(const SPIRType &type, SPIRType::BaseType physical_basetype,
 	                                  const std::string &expr);
 	uint32_t build_msl_interpolant_type(uint32_t type_id, bool is_noperspective);
+	bool uses_pull_model_interpolation(uint32_t id, bool is_sample, bool is_flat) const;
+	std::string default_interpolation_method(bool is_centroid, bool is_sample);
 
 	bool suppress_missing_prototypes = false;
 	bool suppress_incompatible_pointer_types_discard_qualifiers = false;
